        <pluginType>Topic</pluginType>
        <scope>Evaluate Retail Readiness assesses whether a candidate retail location is ready to proceed to expansion or store opening, by synthesizing demand potential, competitive pressure, financial viability, and on‑ground validation.
It provides a go / caution / hold readiness recommendation backed by explainable signals from Salesforce Data Cloud and Consumer Goods Cloud.
✅ Market Readiness
Is demand strong enough and stable across time?
Does footfall confirm demographic assumptions?
Are growth signals sustained or seasonal?
✅ Competitive Readiness
Is competition density manageable for the category?
Are there recent or temporary competitors not yet reflected in data?
Is the competitive activity intensity rising?
✅ Financial Readiness
Does projected revenue exceed internal thresholds?
Is EBITDA margin healthy for the store format?
Is the payback period within acceptable investment norms?
✅ Execution Readiness
Do visit observations validate AI‑generated insights?
Are there operational or infrastructure risks identified on site?
Is data confidence high enough to proceed?
📤 Outputs (What It Produces)
Retail Readiness Status (Ready / Needs Review / Not Ready)
Primary Drivers (top 3 reasons)
Key Risks or Gaps
Confidence Level (High / Medium / Low)
Recommended Next Action
Proceed with expansion
Conduct additional site validation
Re‑evaluate location or timing

These outputs are written back to Salesforce for:
Executive dashboards
Agentforce follow‑ups
Visit planning or escalation</scope>
